## SQ-BBQW-01 | 18 stonecutter recipes for the wood basins and trays; log tags; block tags
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -n "barbequesdelight" logs/latest.log \| grep -i "error\|exception\|missing\|invalid for block" \| head`; recipe dump `creativedelight:stonecutting/bbq_*_from_logs`; tag probe `#creativedelight:bbq_oak_logs`, `#minecraft:mineable/axe`, `#blockrunner:surface/wood`
@pass No log line; 18 stonecutter recipes (9 basin x2, 9 tray x4), each wood's on its own log tag, oak's on `#creativedelight:bbq_oak_logs`; that tag holds oak logs and modded logs, no spruce/birch/jungle/acacia/dark oak/mangrove logs or crimson/warped stems; the 18 blocks in both block tags; no `bbq_basin_from_logs` / `bbq_tray_from_logs`
@fails unknown dict key in `recipes.js` / `tags.js`; `addMatching` warning
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
bootreject (?i)barbequesdelight.*(error|exception|invalid for block)
> zq rdetail _from_logs
> zq itemtag creativedelight:bbq_oak_logs
> zq blocktag minecraft:mineable/axe
> zq blocktag blockrunner:surface/wood
waitlog blocktag blockrunner:surface/wood 20
count creativedelight:stonecutting/bbq_[a-z_]+_from_logs \{ == 18
reject stonecutting/bbq_(basin|tray)_from_logs
reject itemtag creativedelight:bbq_oak_logs \(\d+\): .*minecraft:(spruce|birch|jungle|acacia|dark_oak|mangrove)_log|minecraft:(crimson|warped)_stem
look basins x2 and trays x4 output; each wood's on its own log tag, oak's on #creativedelight:bbq_oak_logs (oak logs and modded logs); the 18 blocks in mineable/axe and blockrunner:surface/wood

## SQ-BBQW-02 | skewering on a warped basin still works (2 beef, stick, cabbage in the off hand)
@group A
@commands Place `barbequesdelight:basin`, `warped_basin`, `tray`, `crimson_tray`; `/data get block` each; fake player puts a raw beef in the warped basin and skewers with a stick; break each with and without an axe
@pass One `barbequesdelight:basin` / `tray` block entity type on every wood; skewering works on the warped basin; each drops itself both ways
@fails block entity type built with the oak block only
@from batches/r1115/p6_a1.qb passed
> clear c6b
> setblock 302 -60 370 barbequesdelight:warped_basin[facing=north]{Items:{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:beef",Count:2b}]}}
> zc2 inv 302 -60 370
> pbot hold c6b minecraft:stick 1
> item replace entity c6b weapon.offhand with farmersdelight:cabbage 2
> zc2 useat c6b 302 -60 370 0.75 0.2 0.5 up
sleep 1
> zc2 inv 302 -60 370
> zp inv c6b
waitlog \[zp\] done 20
expect \[zp\] inv c6b: .*barbequesdelight:raw_beef_skewer
> clear c6b
> pbot remove c6b

## SQ-BBQW-03 | mixed-wood trays stack (support=true on the upper two); removing the base block drops the whole stack
@group A
@commands `/setblock` an air gap, then a `spruce_tray` hanging, an `oak_tray` on it, a `birch_tray` on that; break the spruce tray's support
@pass Mixed trays stack (`support=true` on the upper two); removing the base drops the whole stack
@fails `TrayBlock` still checks `is(this)`
@from batches/r1113/fix_c2a1.qb
> setblock 310 -60 370 minecraft:oak_planks
> setblock 310 -59 370 barbequesdelight:spruce_tray[facing=north]
> zp sneak c2b on
> pbot hold c2b barbequesdelight:tray 1
> pbot use c2b 310 -59 370 up
> pbot hold c2b barbequesdelight:birch_tray 1
> pbot use c2b 310 -58 370 up
> zp sneak c2b off
sleep 1
> zc2 state 310 -59 370
> zc2 state 310 -58 370
> zc2 state 310 -57 370
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x=306,y=-62,z=366,dx=8,dy=10,dz=8]
> setblock 310 -60 370 minecraft:air
sleep 2
> zc2 state 310 -59 370
> zc2 state 310 -58 370
> zc2 state 310 -57 370
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x=306,y=-62,z=366,dx=8,dy=10,dz=8]
expect \[zc2\] state 310 -58 370: .*barbequesdelight:tray\}.*support=true
expect \[zc2\] state 310 -57 370: .*birch_tray.*support=true
look first three states: spruce support=false, oak (barbequesdelight:tray) and birch support=true; after the plank goes all three air and the last kill line says "Killed 3". If the birch use placed at -58 again (the oak use PASSed without placing), BATCH-FAULT: place by hand in a client
> clear c2b

